Test diamond Si with one additional spin-up electron, nspin=2, symmetry=on.

Reference convergence (2026-10-28)
----------------------------------
The former loose SCF settings gave solver-dependent energies, occupations,
forces and stresses. The revised input uses a real-space charge residual
of 1e-8 and limits the adaptive diagonalization threshold to 1e-12 from
the first electronic iteration. Inner and outer iteration budgets are 300.
The default CG solver, random initial wavefunctions, seed 1, structure,
pseudopotential, cutoffs, band count, k points and smearing are unchanged.
The system still contains nine electrons with nupdown=1.

Independent MPI4 calculations with the revised settings:

  Solver   Energy (eV)           Force sum (eV/Angstrom)   Stress sum (kbar)
  CG       -203.7827845743456    8.011022                  2586.655021
  Davidson -203.7827845742895    8.011010                  2586.655301
  PPCG     -203.7827845740013    8.011012                  2586.655295

The reference energy and force/stress sums come from the independent CG
run. Other reference fields and the existing acceptance limits (1e-7 eV,
1e-4 eV/Angstrom and 1e-3 kbar) are unchanged.

With the new reference, CG/Davidson/PPCG at each of 1/2/4 MPI ranks pass
all 63 official property checks. All nine SCF calculations converge.
Across these runs the energy, force-sum and stress-sum spans are
2.350e-9 eV, 1.2e-5 eV/Angstrom and 2.91e-4 kbar. Independently summing
the final weighted occupations gives five spin-up and four spin-down
electrons. Each PPCG run reports one residual warning in the first
electronic iteration; no residual warning occurs at the final step.

The new reference energy is 7.75852e-4 eV higher than the old loose-CG
reference. This revision verifies a reproducible constrained SCF solution
for the fixed initial settings; it does not establish a unique lowest-energy
state. Tighter Davidson/PPCG diagnostics approach the same state. Some
more stringent CG diagnostics fail to converge or exit abnormally and
are excluded from reference generation.

Validation: GNU 12.3, OpenMPI 5.0.10, CPU Release, one OpenMP/OpenBLAS/MKL
thread. Executable SHA-256:
bdf544c3e792c5ce7ea973e32ab093dffa563c09ce76956fbbfcf582d1a5eecf.
To reproduce, use clean case copies with ks_solver=cg, dav and ppcg,
and run the original Autotest.sh at -n1, -n2 and -n4 with -o1.
